  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle strips of sirloin with garlic powder to taste. In a large skillet over medium heat, heat the oil and brown the seasoned beef strips. Transfer to a slow cooker. Cook on high for 3 to 4 hours or on low for 6 to 8 hours.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Then mix bouillon cube with hot water until dissolved, and mix in cornstarch until dissolved. Pour into the slow cooker with meat. Stir in onion, stewed tomatoes, garlic and sugar.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Saute green peppers separately to desired tenderness and add just prior to serving.",
      "group": null
    }
